| R20-GPT-05 | A | P2 | `release/tools/integrity.mjs:250–275`; `release/tools/pre-handoff-check.mjs:250–259`; `release/tests/local-fixture.mjs:286–301` | **R19b does not compose with the required copy deck.** A script-opened dialog containing approved `data-copy-slot` text adds a visible slot when scripted and lacks it when JavaScript is off. `compareIntegrity` therefore returns INCOMPLETE before the contrast exception can make the state usable. Executed in-memory reproduction: `requiresScriptCheck.valid:true`, but `compareIntegrity.pass:false` with a content difference. This exposes a conflict between R19b and round-13 **N13/N14**. The “full-run” fixture inserts unslotted `<p>Dialog text</p>` and checks the dialog’s integrity/axe subresults; it never asserts the complete `stateResult.pass`, including copy compliance. | Define the non-default script-only policy consistently with N13/N14: specify and validate the no-script fallback/baseline, preserve default/shared-content equivalence, and limit any authorized state distinction to verified state-only content. Do not introduce a blanket content waiver. Replace the fixture’s unslotted dialog with approved slots, realistic dialog controls and matching frame evidence; assert the complete state result, not only integrity and axe subresults. |
| R20-GPT-06 | B | P2 | `release/references/critic-rubric.md:30`; `release/references/design-quality.md:45,66`; `release/tools/handoff-contract.mjs:165–171` | **The mandatory hero test assumes every desktop screen is a promotional page.** “For each page, quote its actual hero line” and fail if unrelated business categories could use it unchanged. Every applicable screen/state requires the corresponding PASS. Expert application screens such as Settings, Sign in and Search results appropriately use familiar task headings and often contain no hero. The literal instruction blocks them or encourages unnecessary promotional copy. No round-13 N item applies. | Add at the start of `critic-rubric.md:30` and qualify the corresponding design-quality rule: **“Apply the company-swap test to promotional hero copy and claims of distinction. Functional screens use clear, familiar headings identifying the task or content; do not require a marketing hero or unique phrasing. When promotional hero content is absent, record `generic-hero` PASS with the screen purpose and evidence of absence. Existing promotional content receives the full specificity check.”** |

